<div id="laserheightprobe_control" class="laserheightprobe-panel lhp-panel" style="display: none;">
  <h4><img class="lhp-logo-sm" src="plugin/laserheightprobe/static/img/octoburn-40.png" alt=""> OctoBurn probe
    <a href="#" class="lhp-tablink" data-bind="click: uiOpenTab">Open OctoBurn <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></h4>
  <p class="laserheightprobe-status">
    <span data-bind="css: {'text-success': probeStatus().reachable, 'text-error': probeStatus().reachable === false}, text: probeStatus().reachable === false ? 'ESP not reachable' : (probeStatus().reachable ? 'ESP ok' : 'ESP ?')"></span>
    &middot; latched <strong data-bind="text: yesNo(probeStatus().latched)"></strong>
    &middot; pin <strong data-bind="text: probeStatus().deployed ? 'down' : 'up'" title="As last commanded: the ESP cannot report the pin"></strong>
  </p>
  <p class="laserheightprobe-compact">
    <span data-bind="text: detectedText, css: {'text-warning': detectedWarning}"></span>
    <button class="btn btn-mini" data-bind="click: detect, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady()" title="Ask the printer what is fitted (M1006, M114, M2002 S1)">Detect</button>
  </p>

  <!-- ko ifnot: isLaser -->
  <div class="alert alert-info laserheightprobe-compact">
    No laser is fitted, so the laser tools are hidden. Heating and 3D prints are allowed.
  </div>
  <!-- /ko -->
  <!-- ko if: isLaser -->

  <!-- ko ifnot: sessionOk -->
  <div class="alert laserheightprobe-compact">
    Tap test needed before Probe here<span data-bind="text: sessionReason() ? ' (' + sessionReason() + ')' : ''"></span>.
  </div>
  <!-- /ko -->
  <!-- ko if: waitingForTap -->
  <div class="alert alert-info laserheightprobe-compact"><strong>Tap the probe pin with a finger now.</strong> 60 s.</div>
  <!-- /ko -->

  <!-- ko if: pickModule -->
  <div class="laserheightprobe-row">
    <select class="input-medium" data-bind="options: modules, optionsText: moduleLabel, optionsValue: 'name', value: selectedModule, enable: canProbe() && !running()" title="M1006 cannot name this laser: pick it"></select>
  </div>
  <!-- /ko -->
  <div class="laserheightprobe-row form-inline">
    <label class="radio inline"><input type="radio" value="point" data-bind="checked: hereArea, enable: !running()"> Point</label>
    <label class="radio inline"><input type="radio" value="square" data-bind="checked: hereArea, enable: !running()"> Square</label>
    <label class="radio inline"><input type="radio" value="diamond" data-bind="checked: hereArea, enable: !running()"> Diamond</label>
    <label class="radio inline"><input type="radio" value="x" data-bind="checked: hereArea, enable: !running()"> X line</label>
    <label class="radio inline"><input type="radio" value="y" data-bind="checked: hereArea, enable: !running()"> Y line</label>
    <label class="radio inline" title="Repeatability: N fine touches over one spot, all kept"><input type="radio" value="repeat" data-bind="checked: hereArea, enable: !running()"> Repeat</label>
    <!-- ko if: hereArea() === 'repeat' -->
    <input type="number" step="1" min="3" max="10" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: hereRepeatN, enable: !running()" title="Touches, 3 to 10"> touches
    <!-- /ko -->
    <!-- ko if: patternArea -->
    <input type="number" step="0.5" min="0.5" max="50" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: hereSquareSize, enable: !running()" title="Size across, mm (0.5 to 50)"> mm,
    <input type="number" step="1" min="2" max="9" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: hereSquareN, enable: !running()" title="Points per side (per line)"> <span data-bind="text: (hereArea() === 'x' || hereArea() === 'y') ? 'points' : 'per side'"></span>
    <!-- /ko -->
  </div>
  <div class="laserheightprobe-row form-inline" data-bind="visible: hereArea() !== 'repeat'">
    From <input type="number" step="0.1" min="0" max="300" class="input-mini" data-bind="value: hereHeight, enable: !running()" title="The object's height above the bed, mm (calipers). Empty: probe from where the head is"> mm above the bed
    <span class="muted" data-bind="text: flatBedZ() === null ? '(no bed yet)' : '(bed Z' + Number(flatBedZ()).toFixed(3) + ')'"></span>
    <button class="btn btn-mini" data-bind="click: useHereAsBed, enable: hereLast() && !running()" title="The last Probe here result was on the bare bed: heights are measured from it">Use last result as bed</button>
  </div>
  <p class="muted laserheightprobe-compact" data-bind="visible: hereArea() !== 'repeat' && String(hereHeight() || '').trim() !== ''">
    With a height: the head drops, pin up, to 6 mm above where that puts the top, probes at most
    9 mm down, then goes back up to where you left it. A touch near the start means the object is
    taller than the height given, and stops.
  </p>
  <div class="laserheightprobe-row">
    <button class="btn btn-primary btn-large" data-bind="click: probeHere, enable: canProbeHere, text: probeButtonText">Probe here</button>
    <button class="btn btn-danger" data-bind="click: abort, enable: running">Abort</button>
    <button class="btn" data-bind="click: tapTest, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady(), css: {'btn-warning': !sessionOk()}">Tap test</button>
  </div>
  <p class="muted laserheightprobe-compact" data-bind="visible: hereArea() === 'point'">
    Jog the pin over the spot, a few mm above it, then Probe here. The head goes down at most
    <span data-bind="text: hereMaxDescent"></span> mm, then back up to where it started. No XY move.
  </p>
  <p class="muted laserheightprobe-compact" data-bind="visible: patternArea">
    Jog the pin over the centre, a few mm above the <strong>highest</strong> part of the area.
    <strong>The head moves in X and Y</strong>, pin up, at that height, and probes
    <span data-bind="text: patternCount"></span> points (<span data-bind="text: {square: 'a square', diamond: 'a square turned 45 degrees, corners out along X and Y', x: 'a line along X only', y: 'a line along Y only'}[hereArea()]"></span>).
    It reports the highest, then goes back to where it started.
  </p>
  <p class="muted laserheightprobe-compact" data-bind="visible: hereArea() === 'repeat'">
    Like Probe here, but takes <span data-bind="text: hereRepeatN"></span> fine touches over the
    same spot and keeps every one, for the probe's repeatability. For the swap figure, do one
    repeat run, swap the head out and back in, and repeat; the tab's calibration section
    compares them with the reference.
  </p>
  <p class="muted laserheightprobe-compact" data-bind="visible: repeatText, text: repeatText"></p>
  <p class="text-error" data-bind="text: panelError, visible: panelError"></p>
  <p class="muted" data-bind="text: message, visible: running"></p>

  <!-- ko if: hereLast -->
  <table class="table table-condensed laserheightprobe-last"><tbody>
    <!-- ko if: hereLast().square -->
    <tr><th>Square</th><td>highest of <span data-bind="text: hereLast().square.hits + '/' + hereLast().square.total"></span>
      in <span data-bind="text: hereLast().square.size"></span> mm, range
      <span data-bind="text: hereLast().square.range.toFixed(3)"></span> mm</td></tr>
    <!-- /ko -->
    <tr><th>Trigger Z</th><td data-bind="text: num(hereLast().z, false)"></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Focus Z</th><td data-bind="text: num(hereLast().focus, false)"></td></tr>
    <tr><th>LightBurn offset</th><td><strong data-bind="text: num(hereLast().lightburn, true)"></strong></td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <!-- /ko -->

  <!-- ko if: hereRows().length -->
  <div class="lhp-history">
  <table class="table table-condensed laserheightprobe-here">
    <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>X</th><th>Y</th><th>Z</th><th>Focus</th><th>Offset</th><th></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody data-bind="foreach: hereRows">
      <tr data-bind="css: {info: is_datum}">
        <td data-bind="text: index + 1"></td>
        <td data-bind="text: x.toFixed(1)"></td>
        <td data-bind="text: y.toFixed(1)"></td>
        <td data-bind="text: z.toFixed(3)"></td>
        <td data-bind="text: $parent.num(focus, false)"></td>
        <td data-bind="text: $parent.num(lightburn, true)"></td>
        <td>
          <!-- ko if: is_datum --><span class="muted">datum</span><!-- /ko -->
          <!-- ko ifnot: is_datum -->
          <button class="btn btn-mini" data-bind="click: function () { $parent.setHereDatum(index); }, enable: $parent.canProbe">Set as datum</button>
          <!-- /ko -->
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  </div>
  <div class="laserheightprobe-row">
    <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: copyHereText">Copy as text</button>
    <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: clearHere, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Clear</button>
    <span class="muted" data-bind="text: hereCopyMessage"></span>
  </div>
  <textarea readonly rows="4" id="laserheightprobe_here_text" class="input-block-level laserheightprobe-text" data-bind="value: hereText"></textarea>
  <p class="muted laserheightprobe-compact">
    Offset = focus here minus focus at the datum; positive means this spot's focus is higher.
    Check the sign once in LightBurn with a +1 mm test layer, beam off.
  </p>
  <!-- /ko -->

  <details class="lhp-panel-details">
  <summary>Pointer and beam offset</summary>
  <div class="laserheightprobe-row">
    <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: togglePointer, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady(), css: {'btn-warning': handPointer}, text: handPointer() ? 'Pointer off' : 'Pointer on'" title="The 10W's own beam at low power, or the 2W IR's crosshair. Only with the laser on the head; off by itself after a few minutes."></button>
    <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: markPin, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady()" title="Probe on the head, its pin on the dot">Pin on dot</button>
    <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: markBeam, enable: canProbe() && !running() && printerReady() && offsetPin()" title="Laser on the head, its pointer on the same dot">Light on dot</button>
  </div>
  <p class="muted laserheightprobe-compact">
    Beam offset: with the probe on, Probe here on a card, deploy the pin, jog down until it is just
    above a marked dot and over it, press <em>Pin on dot</em>. Swap the laser in, power cycle, home
    X Y Z, go to the focus height, <em>Pointer on</em>, jog until the light is on the dot, press
    <em>Light on dot</em>.
  </p>
  <!-- ko if: offsetPin -->
  <p class="laserheightprobe-compact">Pin on the dot at X<span data-bind="text: offsetPin().x.toFixed(3)"></span> Y<span data-bind="text: offsetPin().y.toFixed(3)"></span>.</p>
  <!-- /ko -->
  <!-- ko if: offsetResult -->
  <p class="laserheightprobe-compact">
    <strong data-bind="text: offsetResult().module"></strong> beam offset: dx
    <strong data-bind="text: offsetResult().dx.toFixed(3)"></strong>, dy
    <strong data-bind="text: offsetResult().dy.toFixed(3)"></strong> mm
    <button class="btn btn-mini btn-primary" data-bind="click: saveBeamOffset, enable: canProbe">Save</button>
  </p>
  <!-- /ko -->
  </details>
  <p class="text-error" data-bind="text: laserMessage, visible: laserMessage"></p>

  <div class="btn-group laserheightprobe-row">
    <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { probeButton('deploy'); }, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Deploy</button>
    <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { probeButton('stow'); }, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Stow</button>
    <button class="btn btn-small" data-bind="click: function () { probeButton('reset'); }, enable: canProbe() && !running()">Reset</button>
  </div>
  <!-- /ko -->
</div>
